Revise the ConcIR candidate for the same requirements. The requirements and the frozen contract are authoritative; the feedback is repair context.

<domain_requirements>
A sender and a receiver communicate over a channel, and both occasionally need a shared mutex. Every interleaving must terminate; the receiver must not block on the channel while holding the lock the sender needs. On completion the program must print exactly one line `DONE done=1` and then exit; it must terminate.
</domain_requirements>

<contract>
{
  "name": "channel-deadlock",
  "properties": [
    {
      "kind": "deadlock_free",
      "id": "no-deadlock"
    }
  ],
  "assumptions": {
    "sequential_consistency": true,
    "no_spurious_wakeups": true
  },
  "bounds": {
    "max_threads": 8,
    "max_frames_per_thread": 8,
    "max_states": 20000,
    "max_depth": 64,
    "max_boundary_events": 256
  },
  "allowed_scope": {
    "allow_lock_reorder": true
  }
}
</contract>

